{"lc": 1, "type": "constructor", "id": ["langchain", "schema", "document", "Document"], "kwargs": {"metadata": {"source": "data\\documents\\doc\\psoriasisaustralia.org.au_2026.docx", "filename": "psoriasisaustralia.org.au_2026.docx", "filepath": "data\\documents\\doc\\psoriasisaustralia.org.au_2026.docx", "page": 1, "title": "psoriasisaustralia.org.au_2026.docx", "year": "2026"}, "page_content": "Summary\n\nPhototherapy remains a cornerstone in the management of psoriasis in Australia, offering effective relief for many patients. While it is generally safe, it is important for patients to be fully informed about the potential risks and to undergo treatment under the guidance of a qualified healthcare provider. Advances in phototherapy technology and techniques continue to improve outcomes for people with psoriasis, helping them achieve better control over their condition.\n\nPsoriasis Australia provides the information on this website for information purposes only and it does not constitute medical advice. We recommend seeking medical advice from a trained health professional specific to your needs.", "type": "Document"}}